[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m [response] To solve this problem, we need to use the property of a regular octahedron and the distances from a point to its vertices. A regular octahedron can be thought of as two pyramids with a square base joined at their bases. The vertices of a regular octahedron can be represented in a coordinate system in a way that simplifies the distance calculations.
