[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[I = \frac{120}{20} = 6 \text{ amperes}\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Therefore, the amount of current when the resistor has a resistance of \(20\) ohms is \(\boxed{6}\) amperes.
