[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m The formula for the height of the plant after \(n\) days, given an initial height \(H_0\) and a daily growth rate \(r\), is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ H_n = H_0 \times (1 + r)^n \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m In this case, we know the height after \(n\) days (\(H_n = 452\) cm), the daily growth rate (\(r = 0.05\)), and the number of days (\(n = 14\)). We need to find the initial height (\(H_0\)).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Rearranging the formula to solve for \(H_0\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ H_0 = \frac{H_n}{(1 + r)^n} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
