[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m First, let's calculate the volume of a single cylindrical beaker. The formula for the volume of a cylinder is given by:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ V_{\text{cylinder}} = \pi r^2 h \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m where \( r \) is the radius of the cylinder and \( h \) is the height of the cylinder.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m For the cylindrical beaker:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m - Radius \( r = 3 \) cm
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m - Height \( h = 8 \) cm
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Substituting these values into the formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ V_{\text{cylinder}} = \pi (3)^2 (8) = \pi \times 9 \times 8 = 72\pi \, \text{cm}^3 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Next, we calculate the volume of the spherical tank. The formula for the volume of a sphere is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ V_{\text{sphere}} = \frac{4}{3} \pi r^3 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m where \( r \) is the radius of the sphere.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m For the spherical tank:
