[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ V_{\text{cylinder}} = \pi (3)^2 (8) = \pi \cdot 9 \cdot 8 = 72\pi \, \text{cm}^3 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Next, we calculate the volume of the spherical tank. The formula for the volume of a sphere is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ V_{\text{sphere}} = \frac{4}{3} \pi r^3 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m where \( r \) is the radius of the sphere.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m For our spherical tank:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m - \( r = 6 \) cm
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
