[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Next, we calculate the volume of the spherical tank. The formula for the volume of a sphere is \(V_{sphere} = \frac{4}{3}\pi r^3\), where \(r\) is the radius of the sphere.
