[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m The formula to find the highest power of a prime $p$ dividing $n!$ is given by:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ \left\lfloor \frac{n}{p} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{n}{p^2} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{n}{p^3} \right\rfloor + \cdots \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m where $\left\lfloor x \right\rfloor$ denotes the greatest integer less than or equal to $x$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m For $15!$ and the prime $3$, we calculate:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ \left\lfloor \frac{15}{3} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{15}{3^2} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{15}{3^3} \right\rfloor + \cdots \]
