[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m [response] To solve this problem, we need to apply the triangle inequality theorem, which states that the sum of the lengths of any two sides of a triangle must be greater than the length of the third side.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Given that two sides of the triangle are each 8 units long, let's denote the third side as \(x\). According to the triangle inequality theorem, we have the following conditions:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 1. \(8 + 8 > x\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 2. \(8 + x > 8\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 3. \(8 + x > 8\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m The second and third conditions are always true for any positive \(x\), so we focus on the first condition:
