[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m The volume of a cylinder is given by \(V_{cylinder} = \pi r^2 h\), where \(r\) is the radius and \(h\) is the height. For the cylindrical beaker, this is \(V_{cylinder} = \pi \times 3^2 \times 8 = 72\pi \, \text{cm}^3\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m The volume of a sphere is given by \(V_{sphere} = \frac{4}{3}\pi r^3\). For the spherical tank, this is \(V_{sphere} = \frac{4}{3}\pi \times 6^3 = 288\pi \, \text{cm}^3\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m To find out how many beakers it would take to fill the spherical tank, we divide the volume of the spherical tank by the volume of one beaker:
