[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Given $I=40$ amperes and $R=3$ ohms, we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[V = 40 \times 3 = 120\text{ volts}\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Now, we need to find the current $I$ when $R=20$ ohms, with the voltage remaining constant at $120$ volts.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
