[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m - For $f(g(x))$, we have $g(x) = \frac{-2}{x+1}$, so $f(g(x)) = f\left(\frac{-2}{x+1}\right) = \frac{1 + \frac{-2}{x+1}}{1 - \frac{-2}{x+1}} = \frac{x-1}{x+3}$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m - For $g(f(x))$, we have $f(x) = \frac{1+x}{1-x}$, so $g(f(x)) = g\left(\frac{1+x}{1-x}\right) = \frac{-2}{\frac{1+x}{1-x} + 1} = \frac{-2(1-x)}{1+x+1-x} = \frac{-2(1-x)}{2} = x-1$.
