[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Thus, $\tan A = -8$ (though we only use the magnitude for area calculation). We can find the sides using the Law of Sines and the fact that $\tan B = \frac{3}{2}$ and $\tan C = \frac{1}{2}$ imply certain ratios of the sides. The area of the triangle can be found using the formula $\frac{1}{2}ab\sin C$ or similar, but here we use the tangent values to find the height relative to the base $BC$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
