[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m [response] Given that the units digit of $a$ is $2$ and the units digit of $b$ is $4$, and the greatest common divisor (gcd) of $a$ and $b$ is $6$, we can express $a$ and $b$ as $a = 6m$ and $b = 6n$ where $m$ and $n$ are coprime integers (since gcd$(a,b) = 6$).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Since $a$ ends in $2$, $m$ must end in $1$ or $6$ (as $6 \times 1 = 6$ and $6 \times 6 = 36$, and only these will end in $2$ when multiplied by $6$). Similarly, since $b$ ends in $4$, $n$ must end in $4$ or $9$ (as $6 \times 4 = 24$ and $6 \times 9 = 54$, and only these will end in $4$ when multiplied by $6$).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
