[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Let $AB = a$ and $DC = b$. Since $E$ and $F$ are midpoints, $EF$ is the midsegment of the trapezoid and $EF = \frac{a+b}{2}$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m The area of a trapezoid is given by $\frac{1}{2} \times (base1 + base2) \times height$. Let the height of the trapezoid be $h$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Area of $ABCD = \frac{1}{2} \times (a+b) \times h$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Since $ABEF$ is twice $FECD$, let the area of $FECD = x$, then $ABEF = 2x$ and $2x + x = \frac{1}{2} \times (a+b) \times h$.
