[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m The area of trapezoid $ABCD$ can be split into two parts: $ABEF$ and $FECD$. Given that the area of $ABEF$ is twice the area of $FECD$, we can denote the height of the trapezoid as $h$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m The area of $ABEF$ is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \text{Area}_{ABEF} = \frac{1}{2}h\left(a + \frac{a+b}{2}\right) = \frac{h}{2}\left(\frac{2a + a + b}{2}\right) = \frac{h}{4}(3a + b)
