[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m [response] To find the speed of the particle, we first need to determine the velocity components by differentiating the position components with respect to time $t$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m The position of the particle is given by:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ x(t) = 3 \sin \frac{t}{4} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ y(t) = 3 \cos \frac{t}{4} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Differentiating $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ with respect to $t$:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ \frac{dx}{dt} = 3 \cos \frac{t}{4} \cdot \frac{1}{4} = \frac{3}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ \frac{dy}{dt} = 3 (-\sin \frac{t}{4}) \cdot \frac{1}{4} = -\frac{3}{4} \sin \frac{t}{4} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m The speed of the particle is the magnitude of the velocity vector:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ \text{Speed} = \sqrt{\left( \frac{dx}{dt} \right)^2 + \left( \frac{dy}{dt} \right)^2} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ = \sqrt{\left( \frac{3}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4} \right)^2 + \left( -\frac{3}{4} \sin \frac{t}{4} \right)^2} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ = \sqrt{\left( \frac{3}{4} \right)^2 \left( \cos^2 \frac{t}{4} + \sin^2 \frac{t}{4} \right)} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ = \sqrt{\left( \frac{3}{4} \right)^2 \cdot 1} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ = \sqrt{\frac{9}{16}} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[ = \frac{3}{4} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Thus, the speed of the particle is:
