[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m For a regular octahedron, the sum of the squares of the distances from any point \(P\) to the vertices is constant. Let the vertices be \(A, B, C, D, E, F\) and the distances from \(P\) to these vertices be \(PA, PB, PC, PD, PE, PF\). We know:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[PA^2 + PB^2 + PC^2 + PD^2 + PE^2 + PF^2 = \text{constant}\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Let the unknown distance be \(x\). Then we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[3^2 + 7^2 + 8^2 + 9^2 + 11^2 + x^2 = \text{constant}\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Calculating the known squares:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[3^2 = 9\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[7^2 = 49\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[8^2 = 64\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[9^2 = 81\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[11^2 = 121\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Summing these:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[9 + 49 + 64 + 81 + 121 = 324\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[324 + x^2 = \text{constant}\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Since the sum of the squares of the distances from any point to the vertices of a regular octahedron is constant, and knowing the symmetry and properties of the octahedron, the constant sum of the squares of the distances from any point to the vertices is \(2 \times \text{(sum of squares of distances to any three adjacent vertices)}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m For a regular octahedron, the constant sum of the squares of the distances is \(2 \times (3^2 + 7^2 + 8^2) = 2 \times 113 = 226\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Thus:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[324 + x^2 = 226 + 226 = 452\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[x^2 = 452 - 324 = 128\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 
