[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m [response] Given the complex number \( z = re^{i\theta} \), we have the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \left| 2z + \frac{1}{z} \right| = 1.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m First, express \( z \) and \( \frac{1}{z} \) in terms of \( r \) and \( \theta \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m z = re^{i\theta}, \quad \frac{1}{z} = \frac{1}{r} e^{-i\theta}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Thus,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 2z + \frac{1}{z} = 2re^{i\theta} + \frac{1}{r} e^{-i\theta}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Separate into real and imaginary parts:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m 2re^{i\theta} + \frac{1}{r} e^{-i\theta} = 2r(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta) + \frac{1}{r}(\cos \theta - i \sin \theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m Combine the real and imaginary parts:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1466195)[0m \[
